</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g><g transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 273.06 0)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_nestedsvg" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 0) translate(-0.28,0) translate(0,19.69)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 0.28 -19.69)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.85em;--ltx-fo-height:2.85em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="39.37" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 39.37)" width="39.37"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><img src="2603.10445v1/question.png" id="S1.F1.pic1.g12" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:40/40;" width="40" height="40" alt="Refer to caption"></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 36.38 -11.76)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:12.74em;--ltx-fo-height:1.85em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10.22pt;" height="28.9" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 26.21)" width="180.2"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S1.F1.pic1.18" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_left">
<span id="S1.F1.pic1.18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.F1.pic1.18.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">What if the targeting outputs</span></span>
<span id="S1.F1.pic1.18.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.F1.pic1.18.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">are </span><span id="S1.F1.pic1.18.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">unpromptable</span><span id="S1.F1.pic1.18.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">?</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g><g transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 497.41 0)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_nestedsvg" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 0) translate(-0.28,0) translate(0,19.69)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 0.28 -19.69)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.85em;--ltx-fo-height:2.85em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="39.37" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 39.37)" width="39.37"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><img src="2603.10445v1/bulb.png" id="S1.F1.pic1.g13" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:40/40;" width="40" height="40" alt="Refer to caption"></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 44.26 -11.76)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.3em;--ltx-fo-height:1.85em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10.22pt;" height="28.9" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 26.21)" width="117.34"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S1.F1.pic1.19" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_left">
<span id="S1.F1.pic1.19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.F1.pic1.19.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Prompt-free</span></span>
<span id="S1.F1.pic1.19.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.F1.pic1.19.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"></span><span id="S1.F1.pic1.19.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">&amp; Surrogate-based</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S1.F1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fig. 1</span>: </span><span id="S1.F1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Challenge and our solution for instance unlearning in diffusion models.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">II </span><span id="S2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Problem Formulation</span></h2>

<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS1.4" class="ltx_text">II-A</span> </span><span id="S2.SS1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Diffusion Models</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Diffusion models (DMs) generate samples by adding noise in a forward process and learning to reverse it <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>, <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">48</a>, <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>]</cite>. Let <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the dataset that the diffusion model is trained on. For a real sample <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, the forward process in DDIM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>]</cite> maps <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> at diffusion timestep <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{1,\cdots,T\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{1,\cdots,T\}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}=\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}=\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\alpha}_{t}=\prod_{s=1}^{t}{\alpha_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\alpha}_{t}=\prod_{s=1}^{t}{\alpha_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the cumulative product of the noise scheduler <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\alpha_{s}\}_{s=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\alpha_{s}\}_{s=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The denoising network <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\theta}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\{1,\cdots,T\}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\theta}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\{1,\cdots,T\}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> with parameters <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> is trained to predict the added noise <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. The training objective is typically given by:</p>
<table id="S2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{DM}}=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0},\epsilon,t}\!\left[\|\epsilon-\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t},t)\|^{2}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>DM</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{DM}}=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0},\epsilon,t}\!\left[\|\epsilon-\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t},t)\|^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">After training, new samples are generated by starting with noise at <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> and iteratively denoising. We build upon this DDIM framework to incorporate our unlearning objectives, ensuring the model forgets specific instances while maintaining model integrity.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS2.4" class="ltx_text">II-B</span> </span><span id="S2.SS2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Prompt-based Unlearning for Diffusion Models</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Prompt-based unlearning for DMs focuses on preventing the generation of specific styles such that a certain prompt no longer influences the model output <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>.
Let <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(x|c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(x|c)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the conditional data distribution given a conditional input (prompt) <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>. The forget dataset <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of samples to forget and the remember dataset <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of samples to remember.
The objective of prompt-based unlearning is to find a modified parameters <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> such that:</p>
<table id="S2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta^{\prime}}(\mathcal{D}_{f}|c)=0,~p_{\theta^{\prime}}(D|c)\simeq p_{\theta}(D|c)\quad\forall c,\forall D\subset\mathcal{D}_{r}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta^{\prime}}(\mathcal{D}_{f}|c)=0,~p_{\theta^{\prime}}(D|c)\simeq p_{\theta}(D|c)\quad\forall c,\forall D\subset\mathcal{D}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> is the original parameter of the model and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is the learned distribution.
Typically, <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> comprises images sharing a common characteristic (<span id="S2.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.</span>, artistic style, object) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>, which are to be forgotten, whereas <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> refers to the data which we want to remember.
Consequently, we can easily define a subset of conditional inputs <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(\mathcal{D}_{f}|c)\gg p_{\theta}(\mathcal{D}_{r}|c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(\mathcal{D}_{f}|c)\gg p_{\theta}(\mathcal{D}_{r}|c)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall c\in\mathcal{C}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall c\in\mathcal{C}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(\mathcal{D}_{f}|c)\ll p_{\theta}(\mathcal{D}_{r}|c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≪</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(\mathcal{D}_{f}|c)\ll p_{\theta}(\mathcal{D}_{r}|c)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall c\not\in\mathcal{C}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall c\not\in\mathcal{C}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>. In that case, Eq. <a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ II-B Prompt-based Unlearning for Diffusion Models ‣ II Problem Formulation ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> can be relaxed into:</p>
<table id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\theta^{\prime}}(\mathcal{D}_{f}|c)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\theta^{\prime}}(\mathcal{D}_{f}|c)=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall c\in\mathcal{C}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall c\in\mathcal{C}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\theta^{\prime}}(D|c)\simeq p_{\theta}(D|c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≃</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\theta^{\prime}}(D|c)\simeq p_{\theta}(D|c)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall c\in\mathcal{C}_{r},\forall D\subset\mathcal{D}_{r}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall c\in\mathcal{C}_{r},\forall D\subset\mathcal{D}_{r}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Because concept erasing relies on the presence of a prompt <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> to define the unwanted generation, it is specifically applicable to conditional DMs.</p>
</div>
