low="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="255.3"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.F2.pic1.105" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:18.45em;">
<span id="S2.F2.pic1.105.1" class="ltx_p"></span>
<span id="S2.F2.pic1.105.2" class="ltx_p"><em id="S2.F2.pic1.105.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;">“Barbados flag”,</em><span id="S2.F2.pic1.105.2.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
<span id="S2.F2.pic1.105.3" class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter ltx_ref_self" style="font-size:90%;">grok.com</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fig. 2</span>: </span><span id="S2.F2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Cultural and semantic misrepresentation highlight the need for instance unlearning in commercial generative models.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS3.4" class="ltx_text">II-C</span> </span><span id="S2.SS3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Prompt-free Instance Unlearning for Diffusion Models</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt-free instance unlearning for unconditional DMs. </span>
In this work, we propose a <em id="S2.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">prompt-free instance unlearning</em> method. The key difference to prompt-based unlearning is that we cannot rely on <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> in the case of unconditional DMs. The goal is defined as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S2.E6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">[Forgetting]</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\theta^{\prime}}(\mathcal{D}_{f})=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\theta^{\prime}}(\mathcal{D}_{f})=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S2.E7.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">[Model integrity]</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\theta^{\prime}}(D)\simeq p_{\theta}(D)\quad\forall D\subset\mathcal{D}_{r}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≃</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\theta^{\prime}}(D)\simeq p_{\theta}(D)\quad\forall D\subset\mathcal{D}_{r}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt-free instance in conditional DMs.</span>

While prompt-free instance unlearning has been primarily studied in the context of unconditional DMs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>, <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite>, its application in conditional DMs has remained relatively limited. However, we show that such needs arise in some conditional settings, including Stable Diffusion 3 (SD3) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>. As shown in Fig. <a href="#S2.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ II-B Prompt-based Unlearning for Diffusion Models ‣ II Problem Formulation ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, prompts involving historical figures or national flags can lead to misrepresentations, such as incorrect race or cultural symbols. For example, models have mistakenly depicted the Roman general <span id="S2.SS3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">African</span>us as an <span id="S2.SS3.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">African</span> with dark skin, the Islamic leader <span id="S2.SS3.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Salad</span>in as stacked <span id="S2.SS3.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">salad</span>s, or incorrectly depicted the Barbados flag. These issues cannot be resolved through prompt engineering alone and instead call for instance-level unlearning, emphasizing the importance of prompt-free methods.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">III </span><span id="S3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Related Work and Challenges</span></h2>

<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS1.4" class="ltx_text">III-A</span> </span><span id="S3.SS1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Related Work</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt-based machine unlearning. </span>
AblCon <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite> and ESD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite> retrain the model to erase target concepts by replacing them with designated mapping concepts.
To maintain model integrity, prior arts fine-tune gradient-based salient weight in a model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>, introduce a regularization inspired by continual learning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>, <a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>, <a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>]</cite>, or adjust linear projections within attention layers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>, <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>. SPM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite> and CPE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite> adopt low-rank adaptation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>]</cite> to selectively erase target concepts.
As a preference optimization problem, DUO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>
directly modifies local image regions containing target concepts using synthesized images, thereby better preserving the model integrity.
Additionally, GIE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>]</cite> and Concept Corrector <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>]</cite> correct image regions containing target concepts by erasing them in image feature space.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt-free machine unlearning. </span>
Research in prompt-free machine unlearning includes methods for non-diffusion <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">57</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>]</cite> and DMs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>, <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite>. These approaches typically define forgetting (Eq. <a href="#S2.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ II-C Prompt-free Instance Unlearning for Diffusion Models ‣ II Problem Formulation ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) and remembering (Eq. <a href="#S2.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ II-C Prompt-free Instance Unlearning for Diffusion Models ‣ II Problem Formulation ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) objectives and address them with remember loss <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{r}(\mathcal{D}_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{r}(\mathcal{D}_{r})</annotation></semantics></math> and forget loss <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{f}(\mathcal{D}_{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{f}(\mathcal{D}_{f})</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">NegGrad <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite> employs a loss function of the form <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{r}-\lambda\mathcal{L}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{r}-\lambda\mathcal{L}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>, aiming to minimize <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> while maximizing <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>. However, this often leads to a significant conflict between <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\lambda\mathcal{L}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\lambda\mathcal{L}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>, making it difficult to find a balanced optimum. SISS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite> combines two objectives in a single pass via importance sampling from a mixture distribution. However, they still face conflicts similar to  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite> due to their reliance on the same core objective. EraseDiff <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite> replaces scalarizing two objectives with an optimization-based meta-learning approach, but it still exhibits limitations in maintaining model integrity. These methods commonly struggle to preserve model integrity, highlighting the need for a better unlearning method.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS2.4" class="ltx_text">III-B</span> </span><span id="S3.SS2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Challenges: The Fundamental Mismatch in Applying Prompt-based to Prompt-free Unlearning</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Several prior works <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>, <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>, <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>, <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite> have explored machine unlearning with a similar objective—to remove specific concepts or images—but they take advantage of prompt distinguishability (<span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.</span>, prompts related to <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">“nudity”</span> and <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">“non-nudity”</span> are used during the unlearning process). Since we are trying to solve Eqs. <a href="#S2.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ II-C Prompt-free Instance Unlearning for Diffusion Models ‣ II Problem Formulation ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and <a href="#S2.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ II-C Prompt-free Instance Unlearning for Diffusion Models ‣ II Problem Formulation ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, directly applying such works to this problem is not straightforward, and Fig. <a href="#S3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ III-B Challenges: The Fundamental Mismatch in Applying Prompt-based to Prompt-free Unlearning ‣ III Related Work and Challenges ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> illustrates this challenge. Prompt-based unlearning benefits from conditional inputs <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, as the forget dataset <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> is usually highly correlated to a certain set <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, by performing unlearning for a specific <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> as illustrated in (a), one can successfully achieve unlearning with model integrity. However, in (b) instance unlearning, it is ideal not to harm <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\not\in\mathcal{D}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\not\in\mathcal{D}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> (see (b)-above). Therefore, the methods in (a) do not directly apply to the case in (b).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To the best of our knowledge, only a few methods <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>, <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite> aim at truly prompt-free instance unlearning. Image-based unlearning works <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>, <a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>, <a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>]</cite> were exploited prompts. For example, DUO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite> guides unlearning via different prompts to <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, such as <span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">“naked woman”</span> and <span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">“dressed woman”</span>, respectively.
When applying DUO to prompt-free unlearning, it cannot provide guidance using different prompts, failing to preserve model integrity as shown in Fig. <a href="#S1.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ I Introduction ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F3" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S3.F3.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S3.F3.sf1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="230.15" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 221.83 230.15" width="221.83"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,230.15) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(6.73,0) translate(0,-0.28)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 0.28 0.28)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:15.53em;--ltx-fo-height:16.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="230.15" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 230.15)" width="214.82"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><img src="2603.10445v1/cond.png" id="S3.F3.sf1.pic1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:215/230;" width="215" height="230" alt="Refer to caption"></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 102.18 186.83)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 26.9)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 16.41)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 18.29)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 7.26)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.97em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.17em;font-size:7.97pt;" height="8.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="76.84"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F3.sf1.pic1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">where <math id="S3.F3.sf1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x)</annotation></semantics></math> changes </span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 16.42)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.28em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.17em;font-size:7.97pt;" height="8.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="91.34"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F3.sf1.pic1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Before Unlearning </span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 25.03)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.43em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.17em;font-size:7.97pt;" height="8.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="81.94"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F3.sf1.pic1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">After Unlearning</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 192.03 8.56)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.57em;--ltx-fo-height:0.43em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.96" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.96)" width="7.91"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.F3.sf1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 7.78 181.58)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.43em;--ltx-fo-height:0.43em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.96" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.96)" width="5.99"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.F3.sf1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -2.12 96.45)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.24em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="17.17"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.F3.sf1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 94.51 11.09)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.28em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="17.74"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.F3.sf1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F3.sf1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">((a))</span> </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S3.F3.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S3.F3.sf2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="230.15" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 214.82 230.15" width="214.82"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,230.15) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(-0.28,0) translate(0,-0.28)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 0.28 0.28)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:15.53em;--ltx-fo-height:16.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="230.15" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 230.15)" width="214.82"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><img src="2603.10445v1/uncond.png" id="S3.F3.sf2.pic1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:215/230;" width="215" height="230" alt="Refer to caption"></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 28.28 119.77)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.14em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="29.6"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F3.sf2.pic1.1" class="ltx_text">Ideal</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 22.89 13.65)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.92em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="40.36"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F3.sf2.pic1.2" class="ltx_text">Actual</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 192.03 15.48)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.57em;--ltx-fo-height:0.43em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.96" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.96)" width="7.91"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.F3.sf2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 192.03 121.6)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.57em;--ltx-fo-height:0.43em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.96" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.96)" width="7.91"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.F3.sf2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 121.68 10.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.09em;--ltx-fo-height:0.43em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.96)" width="15.08"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.F3.sf2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{f}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F3.sf2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">((b))</span> </span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
