</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">IV </span><span id="S4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Methods</span></h2>

<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS1.4" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span> </span><span id="S4.SS1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Unlearning Methods</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Surrogate-based forgetting objective.</span>
Remembering objective Eq. <a href="#S2.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ II-C Prompt-free Instance Unlearning for Diffusion Models ‣ II Problem Formulation ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> ensures the model integrity on <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. Denoting the forward process of an element <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{r}\in\mathcal{D}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{r}\in\mathcal{D}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}^{r}=\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}x_{0}^{r}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}^{r}=\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}x_{0}^{r}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, a common approach is to adopt the training loss Eq. <a href="#S2.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ II-A Diffusion Models ‣ II Problem Formulation ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> on <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{r}=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}^{r},\epsilon,t}\left[\left\|\epsilon-\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{r},t)\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{r}=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}^{r},\epsilon,t}\left[\left\|\epsilon-\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{r},t)\right\|_{2}^{2}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{r}\sim\mathcal{D}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{r}\sim\mathcal{D}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\sim\text{Uniform}(0,T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Uniform</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\sim\text{Uniform}(0,T)</annotation></semantics></math>.
In comparison, the forgetting objective Eq. <a href="#S2.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ II-C Prompt-free Instance Unlearning for Diffusion Models ‣ II Problem Formulation ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> is designed to disturb the generation of data in <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Our method builds on the idea that, since DMs learn to map between two distributions, small perturbations to the noise can lead the model to forget specific data. Revisiting Eq. <a href="#S2.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ II-A Diffusion Models ‣ II Problem Formulation ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> for the case of remembering data <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, the noise term <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as:</p>
<table id="S4.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=\dfrac{x_{t}^{r}-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}x_{0}^{r}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=\dfrac{x_{t}^{r}-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}x_{0}^{r}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Recalling that DM training aims to map <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, we hypothesize that perturbing this mapping for <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}^{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>f</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}^{f}</annotation></semantics></math> can lead to successful unlearning of the instance, which corresponds to the forgetting target <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>f</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{f}</annotation></semantics></math>. To accomplish this, we propose adjusting <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> by perturbing <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>f</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{f}</annotation></semantics></math> to a surrogate. Specifically, we construct surrogate data that closely resembles the target data while exhibiting distinct characteristics. Using the surrogate data <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>s</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define a modified <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{\prime}(x_{t}^{f},x_{0}^{s})=\dfrac{x_{t}^{f}-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}x_{0}^{s}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>f</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>f</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{\prime}(x_{t}^{f},x_{0}^{s})=\dfrac{x_{t}^{f}-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}x_{0}^{s}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Replacing <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in place of <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> in the remembering objective, we define the forget loss as follows, with <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{s}\sim\mathcal{D}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{s}\sim\mathcal{D}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{f}=\mathbb{E}_{(x_{0}^{f},x_{0}^{s}),t}\|\epsilon^{\prime}-\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{f},t)\|_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>f</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>f</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{f}=\mathbb{E}_{(x_{0}^{f},x_{0}^{s}),t}\|\epsilon^{\prime}-\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{f},t)\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Timestep-aware weighting.</span>
Based on the analysis of the sampling process of DMs proposed in Diff-Tuning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite>, we propose to use an adaptive <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> that effectively balances the two objectives of remembering and forgetting. Since early timesteps affect fine details <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">ma2024deepcache</span>, <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">jeong2025upsample</span>]</cite>, we emphasize <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, while later timesteps focus on generic shape and therefore <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> is emphasized. Specifically, we define <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(t)=1-\beta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(t)=1-\beta t</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> as a hyperparameter. This dynamic weighting strategy effectively balances the two objectives.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gradient surgery.</span>
It is prevalent to resolve conflict of the gradients from the different losses, not only in machine unlearning studies <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>, <a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">61</a>]</cite>, but also more general multi-task optimization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">62</a>, <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">63</a>]</cite>. We also resolve destructive interference between two conflicting gradients by projecting one (<math id="S4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\mathcal{L}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\mathcal{L}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>) onto the other (<math id="S4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\mathcal{L}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\mathcal{L}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>) as follows:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g_{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E12.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\lambda\nabla\mathcal{L}_{r},\quad g_{f}=(1-\lambda)\nabla\mathcal{L}_{f}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lambda\nabla\mathcal{L}_{r},\quad g_{f}=(1-\lambda)\nabla\mathcal{L}_{f},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad g_{f}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad g_{f}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{cases}g_{f}-\mathrm{proj}_{g_{r}}^{g_{f}},&amp;\textnormal{if}\quad g_{r}\cdot g_{f}&lt;0,\\
g_{f},&amp;\textnormal{otherwise.}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>proj</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise.</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{cases}g_{f}-\mathrm{proj}_{g_{r}}^{g_{f}},&amp;\textnormal{if}\quad g_{r}\cdot g_{f}&lt;0,\\
g_{f},&amp;\textnormal{otherwise.}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">This strategy, inspired by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>, is especially beneficial for instance unlearning, where forgetting and retaining objectives directly compete. In our case, <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=g_{r}+g_{f}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=g_{r}+g_{f}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is the final gradient. This surgery refines the unlearning process and further improves generation stability. The overall framework is illustrated in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ IV-A Unlearning Methods ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Prompt-free Instance Unlearning</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.3" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
            Denoising network <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, forget dataset <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>, remember dataset <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, total iterations <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, learning rate <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, max timestep <math id="alg1.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, timestep-aware weighting hyperparameter <math id="alg1.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
            <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{f}\in\mathcal{D}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>f</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{f}\in\mathcal{D}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              Construct surrogate image <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>s</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{s}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>f</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{f}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math>  <a href="#S4.SS3" title="IV-C Surrogate Dataset Construction ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV-C</span></a>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              <span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=1,\dots,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=1,\dots,N</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
               Sample remember image <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{r}\in\mathcal{D}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{r}\in\mathcal{D}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
               <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\sim\text{Uniform}(1,T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Uniform</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\sim\text{Uniform}(1,T)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
               <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
               <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}^{r}\leftarrow\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}x_{0}^{r}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}^{r}\leftarrow\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}x_{0}^{r}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
               <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}^{f}\leftarrow\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}x_{0}^{f}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>f</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>f</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}^{f}\leftarrow\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}x_{0}^{f}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
               <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{r}\leftarrow||\epsilon-\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{r},t)||_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{r}\leftarrow||\epsilon-\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{r},t)||_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg1.l10.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Remember loss
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
               <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{\prime}\leftarrow\frac{x_{t}^{f}-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}x_{0}^{s}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>f</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{\prime}\leftarrow\frac{x_{t}^{f}-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}x_{0}^{s}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l11.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Eq. <a href="#S4.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ IV-A Unlearning Methods ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>
</span>
</div>
