</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS2.4" class="ltx_text">IV-B</span> </span><span id="S4.SS2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Surrogate vs. Exact Unlearning: A Theoretical View</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we explain our method (using a surrogate) is better for preserving the original mapping even than exact unlearning. We consider a simple ridge-regression setting to illustrate how the learned parameter <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> changes when (1) <em id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">removing</em> a single data point <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i},y_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i},y_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> (exact unlearning) vs. (2) <em id="S4.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">replacing</em> it with a surrogate <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i}^{\prime},y_{i}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i}^{\prime},y_{i}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Below, we state Theorems <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Exact Unlearning, restated from []). ‣ IV-B Surrogate vs. Exact Unlearning: A Theoretical View ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>–<a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Surrogate-based Unlearning). ‣ IV-B Surrogate vs. Exact Unlearning: A Theoretical View ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> with proofs and interpretations. Note that <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Exact Unlearning, restated from []). ‣ IV-B Surrogate vs. Exact Unlearning: A Theoretical View ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> was proven long ago by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">64</a>]</cite>, with no novelty on our part. We restate it in our notation solely for alignment with Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Surrogate-based Unlearning). ‣ IV-B Surrogate vs. Exact Unlearning: A Theoretical View ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and Corollary <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Corollary 3 (Comparison). ‣ IV-B Surrogate vs. Exact Unlearning: A Theoretical View ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Exact Unlearning, restated from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">64</a>]</cite>)<span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the parameter vector obtained by solving the ridge-regression problem:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}=\arg\min_{\theta}\Bigl\{\tfrac{1}{2}\|X\theta-y\|^{2}+\tfrac{\lambda}{2}\|\theta\|^{2}\Bigr\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>θ</mi></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}=\arg\min_{\theta}\Bigl\{\tfrac{1}{2}\|X\theta-y\|^{2}+\tfrac{\lambda}{2}\|\theta\|^{2}\Bigr\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote</span></p>
<table id="S4.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=X^{T}X+\lambda I," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=X^{T}X+\lambda I,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">so that</span></p>
<table id="S4.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}=A^{-1}X^{T}y." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}=A^{-1}X^{T}y.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Now remove the <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th row <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(x_{i},y_{i}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(x_{i},y_{i}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,y</annotation></semantics></math>, producing <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{X},\widetilde{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{X},\widetilde{y}</annotation></semantics></math>. The new solution, trained from scratch on <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{X},\widetilde{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{X},\widetilde{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, is</span></p>
<table id="S4.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\theta}=\arg\min_{\theta}\Bigl\{\tfrac{1}{2}\|\widetilde{X}\theta-\widetilde{y}\|^{2}+\tfrac{\lambda}{2}\|\theta\|^{2}\Bigr\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>θ</mi></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\theta}=\arg\min_{\theta}\Bigl\{\tfrac{1}{2}\|\widetilde{X}\theta-\widetilde{y}\|^{2}+\tfrac{\lambda}{2}\|\theta\|^{2}\Bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, the difference between the two solutions satisfies the following closed-form expression:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\theta}-\theta^{*}=\frac{\bigl(x_{i}^{T}\theta^{*}-y_{i}\bigr)}{1-x_{i}^{T}A^{-1}x_{i}}A^{-1}x_{i}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\theta}-\theta^{*}=\frac{\bigl(x_{i}^{T}\theta^{*}-y_{i}\bigr)}{1-x_{i}^{T}A^{-1}x_{i}}A^{-1}x_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is the feature vector of the removed row, and <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{-1}x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{-1}x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the direction in parameter space that adjusts for removing <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i},y_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i},y_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thminterpretationx1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_interpretation">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thminterpretationx1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Interpretation</span></span><span id="Thminterpretationx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thminterpretationx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thminterpretationx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Exact unlearning strictly removes the data point’s influence, but it may cause a larger shift in the solution because <math id="Thminterpretationx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\theta}-\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\theta}-\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is fully determined by that row’s removal.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the minimizer of the ridge objective, it satisfies</span></p>
<table id="S4.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(X^{T}X+\lambda I\bigr)\theta^{*}=X^{T}y," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(X^{T}X+\lambda I\bigr)\theta^{*}=X^{T}y,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">or equivalently <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\theta^{*}=X^{T}y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\theta^{*}=X^{T}y</annotation></semantics></math>.
Removing row <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> yields <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{X},\widetilde{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{X},\widetilde{y}</annotation></semantics></math>. One checks:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{X}^{T}\widetilde{X}=X^{T}X-x_{i}x_{i}^{T},\quad\widetilde{X}^{T}\widetilde{y}=X^{T}y-x_{i}y_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{X}^{T}\widetilde{X}=X^{T}X-x_{i}x_{i}^{T},\quad\widetilde{X}^{T}\widetilde{y}=X^{T}y-x_{i}y_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">The new solution <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="S4.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(\widetilde{X}^{T}\widetilde{X}+\lambda I\bigr)\widetilde{\theta}=\widetilde{X}^{T}\widetilde{y}\Longleftrightarrow\bigl(A-x_{i}x_{i}^{T}\bigr)\widetilde{\theta}=A\theta^{*}-x_{i}y_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(\widetilde{X}^{T}\widetilde{X}+\lambda I\bigr)\widetilde{\theta}=\widetilde{X}^{T}\widetilde{y}\Longleftrightarrow\bigl(A-x_{i}x_{i}^{T}\bigr)\widetilde{\theta}=A\theta^{*}-x_{i}y_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Let us express <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> via a rank-1 update. To this end,
Let</span></p>
<table id="S4.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=x_{i}x_{i}^{T},\quad v=x_{i}y_{i},\quad\alpha=x_{i}^{T}\theta^{*}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=x_{i}x_{i}^{T},\quad v=x_{i}y_{i},\quad\alpha=x_{i}^{T}\theta^{*}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">Then <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as</span></p>
<table id="S4.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A-U)^{-1}(A\theta^{*}-v)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A-U)^{-1}(A\theta^{*}-v).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">Subtract <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, insert <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> in a convenient form, and simplify:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E24X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E24X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\theta}-\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\theta}-\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E24X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(A-U)^{-1}(A\theta^{*}-v)-\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(A-U)^{-1}(A\theta^{*}-v)-\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E24Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E24Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(A-U)^{-1}\Bigl[(A\theta^{*}-v)-(A-U)\theta^{*}\Bigr]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(A-U)^{-1}\Bigl[(A\theta^{*}-v)-(A-U)\theta^{*}\Bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">Observe that <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A-U)\theta^{*}=A\theta^{*}-x_{i}x_{i}^{T}\theta^{*}=X^{T}y-x_{i}\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A-U)\theta^{*}=A\theta^{*}-x_{i}x_{i}^{T}\theta^{*}=X^{T}y-x_{i}\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence</span></p>
<table id="S4.E25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E25X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E25X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(A\theta^{*}-v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(A\theta^{*}-v)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E25X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-(A\theta^{*})+U\theta^{*}=-v+U\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-(A\theta^{*})+U\theta^{*}=-v+U\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E25Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E25Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{i}\alpha-x_{i}y_{i}=x_{i}(\alpha-y_{i})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{i}\alpha-x_{i}y_{i}=x_{i}(\alpha-y_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p2.8.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="S4.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\theta}-\theta^{*}=(A-x_{i}x_{i}^{T})^{-1}\Bigl[x_{i}(\alpha-y_{i})\Bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\theta}-\theta^{*}=(A-x_{i}x_{i}^{T})^{-1}\Bigl[x_{i}(\alpha-y_{i})\Bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p2.9.1" class="ltx_text">Applying the Sherman–Morrison (rank-1) inverse lemma tells us</span></p>
<table id="S4.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A-x_{i}x_{i}^{T})^{-1}x_{i}=\frac{1}{1-x_{i}^{T}A^{-1}x_{i}}A^{-1}x_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A-x_{i}x_{i}^{T})^{-1}x_{i}=\frac{1}{1-x_{i}^{T}A^{-1}x_{i}}A^{-1}x_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p2.10.1" class="ltx_text">Finally,</span></p>
<table id="S4.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\theta}-\theta^{*}=\frac{(\alpha-y_{i})}{1-x_{i}^{T}A^{-1}x_{i}}A^{-1}x_{i}=\frac{\bigl(x_{i}^{T}\theta^{*}-y_{i}\bigr)}{1-x_{i}^{T}A^{-1}x_{i}}A^{-1}x_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\theta}-\theta^{*}=\frac{(\alpha-y_{i})}{1-x_{i}^{T}A^{-1}x_{i}}A^{-1}x_{i}=\frac{\bigl(x_{i}^{T}\theta^{*}-y_{i}\bigr)}{1-x_{i}^{T}A^{-1}x_{i}}A^{-1}x_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p2.11.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the derivation.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Surrogate-based Unlearning)<span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,y,\lambda,\theta^{*},A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,y,\lambda,\theta^{*},A</annotation></semantics></math> the same to the <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Exact Unlearning, restated from []). ‣ IV-B Surrogate vs. Exact Unlearning: A Theoretical View ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
Suppose we modify exactly one row <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(x_{i},y_{i}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(x_{i},y_{i}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math> to a new (surrogate) pair <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(x_{i}^{\prime},y_{i}^{\prime}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(x_{i}^{\prime},y_{i}^{\prime}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the new design/label set:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\dagger}=X+e_{i}(x_{i}^{\prime}-x_{i})^{T},\quad y^{\dagger}=y+e_{i}(y_{i}^{\prime}-y_{i})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\dagger}=X+e_{i}(x_{i}^{\prime}-x_{i})^{T},\quad y^{\dagger}=y+e_{i}(y_{i}^{\prime}-y_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th standard basis vector. The new ridge solution is</span></p>
<table id="S4.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\dagger}=\arg\min_{\theta}\Bigl\{\tfrac{1}{2}\|X^{\dagger}\theta-y^{\dagger}\|^{2}+\tfrac{\lambda}{2}\|\theta\|^{2}\Bigr\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>θ</mi></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\dagger}=\arg\min_{\theta}\Bigl\{\tfrac{1}{2}\|X^{\dagger}\theta-y^{\dagger}\|^{2}+\tfrac{\lambda}{2}\|\theta\|^{2}\Bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then the following holds.</span></p>
<table id="S4.E31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E31X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E31X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\theta^{\dagger}-\theta^{*}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\theta^{\dagger}-\theta^{*}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E31X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(A+M)^{-1}\bigl[X^{T}y+x_{i}(y_{i}^{\prime}-y_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>X</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(A+M)^{-1}\bigl[X^{T}y+x_{i}(y_{i}^{\prime}-y_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E31Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E31Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+(x_{i}-x_{i}^{\prime})y_{i}^{\prime}\bigr]-A^{-1}X^{T}y," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>X</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+(x_{i}-x_{i}^{\prime})y_{i}^{\prime}\bigr]-A^{-1}X^{T}y,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<table id="S4.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=x_{i}(x_{i}^{\prime}-x_{i})^{T}+(x_{i}^{\prime}-x_{i})x_{i}^{T}+(x_{i}^{\prime}-x_{i})(x_{i}^{\prime}-x_{i})^{T}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=x_{i}(x_{i}^{\prime}-x_{i})^{T}+(x_{i}^{\prime}-x_{i})x_{i}^{T}+(x_{i}^{\prime}-x_{i})(x_{i}^{\prime}-x_{i})^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thminterpretationx2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_interpretation">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thminterpretationx2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Interpretation</span></span><span id="Thminterpretationx2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thminterpretationx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thminterpretationx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By introducing a surrogate row <math id="Thminterpretationx2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(x_{i}^{\prime},y_{i}^{\prime}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(x_{i}^{\prime},y_{i}^{\prime}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>, we adjust the model less drastically if <math id="Thminterpretationx2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently close to <math id="Thminterpretationx2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. This allows the unlearning effect (on <math id="Thminterpretationx2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>) while partially preserving the original parameter <math id="Thminterpretationx2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">We have</span></p>
<table id="S4.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=X^{T}X+\lambda I,\quad\theta^{*}=A^{-1}X^{T}y." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=X^{T}X+\lambda I,\quad\theta^{*}=A^{-1}X^{T}y.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">For simplicity, let:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=x_{i}^{\prime}-x_{i},\quad s=y_{i}^{\prime}-y_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=x_{i}^{\prime}-x_{i},\quad s=y_{i}^{\prime}-y_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Then the update can be written as</span></p>
<table id="S4.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\dagger}=X+e_{i}r^{T},\quad y^{\dagger}=y+e_{i}s." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\dagger}=X+e_{i}r^{T},\quad y^{\dagger}=y+e_{i}s.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">The new solution <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the ridge normal equation:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl({X^{\dagger}}^{T}X^{\dagger}+\lambda I\bigr)\theta^{\dagger}={X^{\dagger}}^{T}y^{\dagger}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>X</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>X</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl({X^{\dagger}}^{T}X^{\dagger}+\lambda I\bigr)\theta^{\dagger}={X^{\dagger}}^{T}y^{\dagger},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{X^{\dagger}}^{T}X^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>X</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{X^{\dagger}}^{T}X^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> can be computed as</span></p>
<table id="S4.E37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E37X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E37X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\displaystyle X^{\dagger}}^{T}X^{\dagger}=(X+e_{i}r^{T})^{T}(X+e_{i}r^{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>X</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\displaystyle X^{\dagger}}^{T}X^{\dagger}=(X+e_{i}r^{T})^{T}(X+e_{i}r^{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E37Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E37Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=X^{T}X+\underbrace{X^{T}(e_{i}r^{T})+(e_{i}r^{T})^{T}X+(e_{i}r^{T})^{T}(e_{i}r^{T})}_{\text{sum of rank-1 terms}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>sum of rank-1 terms</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=X^{T}X+\underbrace{X^{T}(e_{i}r^{T})+(e_{i}r^{T})^{T}X+(e_{i}r^{T})^{T}(e_{i}r^{T})}_{\text{sum of rank-1 terms}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.7.1" class="ltx_text">One finds:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{T}(e_{i}r^{T})=x_{i}r^{T},(e_{i}r^{T})^{T}X=rx_{i}^{T},(e_{i}r^{T})^{T}(e_{i}r^{T})=rr^{T}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{T}(e_{i}r^{T})=x_{i}r^{T},(e_{i}r^{T})^{T}X=rx_{i}^{T},(e_{i}r^{T})^{T}(e_{i}r^{T})=rr^{T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.8.1" class="ltx_text">Altogether,</span></p>
<table id="S4.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{X^{\dagger}}^{T}X^{\dagger}=X^{T}X+\bigl[x_{i}r^{T}+rx_{i}^{T}+rr^{T}\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>X</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{X^{\dagger}}^{T}X^{\dagger}=X^{T}X+\bigl[x_{i}r^{T}+rx_{i}^{T}+rr^{T}\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.9.1" class="ltx_text">Hence</span></p>
<table id="S4.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E40.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A^{\dagger}={X^{\dagger}}^{T}X^{\dagger}+\lambda I=\underbrace{(X^{T}X+\lambda I)}_{=A}+\underbrace{\bigl[x_{i}r^{T}+rx_{i}^{T}+rr^{T}\bigr]}_{=:M}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>X</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>X</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\dagger}={X^{\dagger}}^{T}X^{\dagger}+\lambda I=\underbrace{(X^{T}X+\lambda I)}_{=A}+\underbrace{\bigl[x_{i}r^{T}+rx_{i}^{T}+rr^{T}\bigr]}_{=:M}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.10.1" class="ltx_text">Using <a href="#S4.E35" title="In Proof. ‣ IV-B Surrogate vs. Exact Unlearning: A Theoretical View ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{X^{\dagger}}^{T}y^{\dagger}=(X+e_{i}r^{T})^{T}(y+e_{i}s)=X^{T}y+\bigl[x_{i}s+ry_{i}^{\prime}\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>X</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{X^{\dagger}}^{T}y^{\dagger}=(X+e_{i}r^{T})^{T}(y+e_{i}s)=X^{T}y+\bigl[x_{i}s+ry_{i}^{\prime}\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.11.1" class="ltx_text">Denote</span></p>
<table id="S4.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=x_{i}s+ry_{i}^{\prime}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=x_{i}s+ry_{i}^{\prime}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.12.1" class="ltx_text">Thus,</span></p>
<table id="S4.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\dagger}=A+M,\quad{X^{\dagger}}^{T}y^{\dagger}=X^{T}y+B." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>X</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\dagger}=A+M,\quad{X^{\dagger}}^{T}y^{\dagger}=X^{T}y+B.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.13.1" class="ltx_text">Hence the new solution is</span></p>
<table id="S4.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\dagger}=\bigl(A+M\bigr)^{-1}\bigl[X^{T}y+B\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\dagger}=\bigl(A+M\bigr)^{-1}\bigl[X^{T}y+B\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.14.1" class="ltx_text">Subtract the old solution <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}=A^{-1}X^{T}y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}=A^{-1}X^{T}y</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\dagger}-\theta^{*}=(A+M)^{-1}\bigl[X^{T}y+B\bigr]-A^{-1}X^{T}y." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\dagger}-\theta^{*}=(A+M)^{-1}\bigl[X^{T}y+B\bigr]-A^{-1}X^{T}y.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.15.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=x_{i}(y_{i}^{\prime}-y_{i})+(x_{i}-x_{i}^{\prime})y_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=x_{i}(y_{i}^{\prime}-y_{i})+(x_{i}-x_{i}^{\prime})y_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#S4.E45" title="In Proof. ‣ IV-B Surrogate vs. Exact Unlearning: A Theoretical View ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a>, we get</span></p>
<table id="S4.E46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E46X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E46X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\theta^{\dagger}-\theta^{*}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\theta^{\dagger}-\theta^{*}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E46X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(A+M)^{-1}\bigl[X^{T}y+x_{i}(y_{i}^{\prime}-y_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>X</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(A+M)^{-1}\bigl[X^{T}y+x_{i}(y_{i}^{\prime}-y_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E46Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E46Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+(x_{i}-x_{i}^{\prime})y_{i}^{\prime}\bigr]-A^{-1}X^{T}y." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>X</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+(x_{i}-x_{i}^{\prime})y_{i}^{\prime}\bigr]-A^{-1}X^{T}y.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.16.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Although it is not straightforward to tell, there are cases in which surrogate-based unlearning preserves the original parameter better than exact unlearning. The following <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Corollary 3 (Comparison). ‣ IV-B Surrogate vs. Exact Unlearning: A Theoretical View ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Corollary</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> enables easier comparison.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Comparison)<span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,y,\lambda,\theta^{*},X^{\dagger},y^{\dagger},\theta^{\dagger},A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,y,\lambda,\theta^{*},X^{\dagger},y^{\dagger},\theta^{\dagger},A</annotation></semantics></math> the same to the <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Surrogate-based Unlearning). ‣ IV-B Surrogate vs. Exact Unlearning: A Theoretical View ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. If <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}=x_{i}^{\prime}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}=x_{i}^{\prime}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}\neq y_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}\neq y_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S4.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\|\widetilde{\theta}-\theta^{*}\|}{\|\theta^{\dagger}-\theta^{*}\|}=\frac{|x_{i}^{T}\theta^{*}-y_{i}|}{|y_{i}^{\prime}-y_{i}||1-x_{i}^{T}A^{-1}x_{i}|}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\|\widetilde{\theta}-\theta^{*}\|}{\|\theta^{\dagger}-\theta^{*}\|}=\frac{|x_{i}^{T}\theta^{*}-y_{i}|}{|y_{i}^{\prime}-y_{i}||1-x_{i}^{T}A^{-1}x_{i}|},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e., surrogate-based unlearning can preserve the original solution more than exact unlearning.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F4" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2603.10445v1/unlearning_comparison.svg" id="S4.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/302;" width="476" height="302"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fig. 4</span>: </span><span id="S4.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Surrogate-based unlearning (<math id="S4.F4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">†</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math>) can be better than exact unlearing (<math id="S4.F4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#005900;" mathcolor="#005900">θ</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>) in mapping preservation, <span id="S4.F4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span>, the line is closer to the original (<math id="S4.F4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Thmtakeawayx1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_takeaway">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtakeawayx1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Takeaway</span></span><span id="Thmtakeawayx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtakeawayx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtakeawayx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S4.F4" title="In IV-B Surrogate vs. Exact Unlearning: A Theoretical View ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> illustrates the results of <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Corollary 3 (Comparison). ‣ IV-B Surrogate vs. Exact Unlearning: A Theoretical View ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Corollary</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> implemented on a simple 1D ridge-regression problem. In this simple example, exact unlearning removes any influence of <math id="Thmtakeawayx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i},y_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i},y_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> at the cost of a potentially larger parameter change. In contrast, if we carefully choose a surrogate <math id="Thmtakeawayx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(x_{i}^{\prime},y_{i}^{\prime}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(x_{i}^{\prime},y_{i}^{\prime}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>, the resulting parameter <math id="Thmtakeawayx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> can stay closer to the original <math id="Thmtakeawayx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. <a href="#S4.SS3" title="IV-C Surrogate Dataset Construction ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV-C</span></a> discusses how to generalize this idea and select practical surrogates.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.8" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">By <a href="#S4.E35" title="In Proof. ‣ IV-B Surrogate vs. Exact Unlearning: A Theoretical View ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a> and the assumption that <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}=x_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}=x_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the definition of <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#S4.E40" title="In Proof. ‣ IV-B Surrogate vs. Exact Unlearning: A Theoretical View ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a>, we have <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Plugging <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}=x_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}=x_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> into <a href="#S4.E46" title="In Proof. ‣ IV-B Surrogate vs. Exact Unlearning: A Theoretical View ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a>, we get</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\theta^{\dagger}-\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\theta^{\dagger}-\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=A^{-1}\bigl[X^{T}y+x_{i}(y_{i}^{\prime}-y_{i})\bigr]-A^{-1}X^{T}y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=A^{-1}\bigl[X^{T}y+x_{i}(y_{i}^{\prime}-y_{i})\bigr]-A^{-1}X^{T}y</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=A^{-1}x_{i}(y_{i}^{\prime}-y_{i})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=A^{-1}x_{i}(y_{i}^{\prime}-y_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking norm to <a href="#S4.E49" title="In Proof. ‣ IV-B Surrogate vs. Exact Unlearning: A Theoretical View ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a> makes</span></p>
<table id="S4.E50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\theta^{\dagger}-\theta^{*}\|=\|A^{-1}x_{i}\||y_{i}^{\prime}-y_{i}|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\theta^{\dagger}-\theta^{*}\|=\|A^{-1}x_{i}\||y_{i}^{\prime}-y_{i}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">and taking norm to <a href="#S4.E18" title="In Theorem 1 (Exact Unlearning, restated from []). ‣ IV-B Surrogate vs. Exact Unlearning: A Theoretical View ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> makes</span></p>
<table id="S4.E51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\widetilde{\theta}-\theta^{*}\|=\frac{|x_{i}^{T}\theta^{*}-y_{i}|}{|1-x_{i}^{T}A^{-1}x_{i}|}\|A^{-1}x_{i}\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\widetilde{\theta}-\theta^{*}\|=\frac{|x_{i}^{T}\theta^{*}-y_{i}|}{|1-x_{i}^{T}A^{-1}x_{i}|}\|A^{-1}x_{i}\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">By the assumption, <a href="#S4.E50" title="In Proof. ‣ IV-B Surrogate vs. Exact Unlearning: A Theoretical View ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a> is nonzero. Dividing <a href="#S4.E51" title="In Proof. ‣ IV-B Surrogate vs. Exact Unlearning: A Theoretical View ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a> by <a href="#S4.E50" title="In Proof. ‣ IV-B Surrogate vs. Exact Unlearning: A Theoretical View ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>, we have <a href="#S4.E47" title="In Corollary 3 (Comparison). ‣ IV-B Surrogate vs. Exact Unlearning: A Theoretical View ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS3.4" class="ltx_text">IV-C</span> </span><span id="S4.SS3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Surrogate Dataset Construction</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Editing tools. </span>

In practice, any mild editing method that modifies only the undesired attributes while preserving the overall structure can serve as a valid surrogate. We employ three different approaches in Fig. <a href="#S4.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ IV-C Surrogate Dataset Construction ‣ IV Methods ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>: TediGAN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">65</a>]</cite> for CelebA, SDEdit <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">66</a>]</cite> for the <em id="S4.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">“Xerxes”</em> case in SD3 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> , and manual painting for the national flags like <em id="S4.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">“Japan flag”</em>. Further discussion on diverse surrogate construction strategies, including noising and flipping, is provided in Table <a href="#S6.T5" title="Table V ‣ VI-A Ablation Studies ‣ VI Discussion ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">V</span></a> and Fig. <a href="#S6.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ VI-B Validation of Using an Edited Image as a Surrogate ‣ VI Discussion ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_4"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S4.F5.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel" height="119" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 119 119" width="119"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,119) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(59.5,0) translate(0,59.5)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -59.5 -59.5)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.6em;--ltx-fo-height:8.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="119" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 119)" width="119"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><img src="2603.10445v1/images/main/edit_example/00000.jpg" id="S4.F5.pic1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:119/119;" width="119" height="119" alt="Refer to caption"></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#D9D9D9;" fill="#D9D9D9" fill-opacity="0.8"><path style="stroke:none" d="M -25.45 42.25 h 50.91 v 15.37 h -50.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="0.8" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -22.69 47.17)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.97em;--ltx-fo-height:0.65em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="46.68"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F5.pic1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To forget</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_4"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S4.F5.pic2" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel" height="119" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 119 119" width="119"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,119) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(59.5,0) translate(0,59.5)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -59.5 -59.5)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.6em;--ltx-fo-height:8.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="119" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 119)" width="119"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><img src="2603.10445v1/images/main/edit_example/sd3_1.jpg" id="S4.F5.pic2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:119/119;" width="119" height="119" alt="Refer to caption"></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#D9D9D9;" fill="#D9D9D9" fill-opacity="0.8"><path style="stroke:none" d="M -25.45 42.25 h 50.91 v 15.37 h -50.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="0.8" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -22.69 47.17)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.97em;--ltx-fo-height:0.65em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="46.68"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F5.pic2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To forget</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_4"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S4.F5.pic3" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel" height="119" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 119 119" width="119"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,119) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(59.5,0) translate(0,59.5)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -59.5 -59.5)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.6em;--ltx-fo-height:8.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="119" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 119)" width="119"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><img src="2603.10445v1/images/main/sd3_figure_down/Japan/target_original.jpg" id="S4.F5.pic3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:119/119;" width="119" height="119" alt="Refer to caption"></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#D9D9D9;" fill="#D9D9D9" fill-opacity="0.8"><path style="stroke:none" d="M -25.45 42.25 h 50.91 v 15.37 h -50.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="0.8" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -22.69 47.17)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.97em;--ltx-fo-height:0.65em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="46.68"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F5.pic3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To forget</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_4"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S4.F5.pic4" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel" height="119" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 119 119" width="119"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,119) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(59.5,0) translate(0,59.5)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -59.5 -59.5)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.6em;--ltx-fo-height:8.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="119" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 119)" width="119"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><img src="2603.10445v1/images/main/edit_example/00000_edit.jpg" id="S4.F5.pic4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:119/119;" width="119" height="119" alt="Refer to caption"></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#D9D9D9;" fill="#D9D9D9" fill-opacity="0.8"><path style="stroke:none" d="M -26.53 42.25 h 53.06 v 15.37 h -53.06 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="0.8" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -23.76 47.17)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.04em;--ltx-fo-height:0.65em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="47.53"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F5.pic4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Surrogate</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S4.F5.pic5" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel" height="119" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 119 119" width="119"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,119) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(59.5,0) translate(0,59.5)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -59.5 -59.5)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.6em;--ltx-fo-height:8.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="119" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 119)" width="119"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><img src="2603.10445v1/images/main/edit_example/sd3_1_edit.jpg" id="S4.F5.pic5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:119/119;" width="119" height="119" alt="Refer to caption"></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#D9D9D9;" fill="#D9D9D9" fill-opacity="0.8"><path style="stroke:none" d="M -26.53 42.25 h 53.06 v 15.37 h -53.06 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="0.8" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -23.76 47.17)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.04em;--ltx-fo-height:0.65em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="47.53"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F5.pic5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Surrogate</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S4.F5.pic6" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel" height="119" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 119 119" width="119"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,119) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(59.5,0) translate(0,59.5)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -59.5 -59.5)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.6em;--ltx-fo-height:8.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="119" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 119)" width="119"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><img src="2603.10445v1/images/main/sd3_figure_down/Japan/target_surrogate.jpg" id="S4.F5.pic6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:119/119;" width="119" height="119" alt="Refer to caption"></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#D9D9D9;" fill="#D9D9D9" fill-opacity="0.8"><path style="stroke:none" d="M -26.53 42.25 h 53.06 v 15.37 h -53.06 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="0.8" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -23.76 47.17)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.04em;--ltx-fo-height:0.65em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="47.53"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F5.pic6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Surrogate</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F5.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fig. 5</span>: </span><span id="S4.F5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Surrogate data construction of (left) CelebA with TediGAN, (middle) SD3 with SDEdit, and (right) manual editing.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Scalability, automation, and flexibility. </span>
These surrogate construction methods are straightforward, efficient, and automatable. Using TediGAN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">65</a>]</cite> or SDEdit <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">66</a>]</cite>, we constructed the surrogate images within five seconds per image with fixed prompts and consistent hyperparameters. This deterministic pipeline ensures scalability to larger datasets. Additionally, manual editing provides a crucial advantage: if a user encounters an undesirable output on their device, they can manually edit the image in just a few seconds, creating a suitable surrogate that prevents future occurrences of similar undesired generations. Our approach accommodates diverse editing techniques, combining automation and flexibility to streamline surrogate data creation efficiently.</p>
</div>
