<div id="S6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Timestep-aware weighting. </span>
Also, we conducted an ablation study testing various <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> for the loss design under two conditions: 1) constant <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, and 2) timestep-aware <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S6.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=1-\beta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=1-\beta t</annotation></semantics></math>).
Experiment is conducted on a single instance and the metrics are evaluated using 10,000 generations.
As shown in Table  <a href="#S6.T3" title="Table III ‣ VI-A Ablation Studies ‣ VI Discussion ‣ Unlearning the Unpromptable: Prompt-free Instance Unlearning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III</span></a>, with <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=1-\beta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=1-\beta t</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=5\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=5\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>, the model achieved the best overall performance.</p>
</div>
